				<div class="et_pb_text_inner"><h2 style="text-align: center;"><strong>Testimonials</strong></h2></div>
			</div><div class="et_pb_module et_pb_code et_pb_code_3">
				
				
				
				
				<div class="et_pb_code_inner"><div class="strong-view strong-view-id-1 modern wpmtst-modern slider-container carousel slider-mode-horizontal slider-adaptive controls-type-sides-outside controls-style-buttons pager-type-full pager-style-buttons nav-position-outside" data-count=8 data-slider-var=strong_slider_id_1 data-state=idle><div class="strong-content wpmslider-content"><div class="wpmtst-testimonial testimonial t-slide post-4537"><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-inner testimonial-inner"><div data-infinite-loop="true"  class="wpmtst-testimonial-content  testimonial-content"><p>The dream of good quality standard, affordable, and nutritionally balanced nutrients is becoming a reality. I give NOUN the credit, without them, I would not have been successful. I gained so much from the teachings and mentorship at the school. I encourage other students to be active in their course of study and most importantly participate fully in the entrepreneurship course &#8211; GST 302.</p></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-image testimonial-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Basilia-150x150.jpeg" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" /></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-name">Irozuru Basilia Ogechukwu </div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-company">Student - South-West, Lagos, Incubatee</div><div class="clear"></div></div></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial testimonial t-slide post-4539"><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-inner testimonial-inner"><div data-infinite-loop="true"  class="wpmtst-testimonial-content  testimonial-content"><p>I appreciate the Directorate for Entrepreneurship and General Studies for encouraging us to become entrepreneurs and for providing conducive environment for production and research. The GST courses and the mentorship received have positively impacted my life especially towards developing and modernizing my business. Now my products are standardized and beautifully packaged. Thank you DE&amp;GS for setting me towards the path of economic independence after graduation.</p></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-image testimonial-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/isa-1-150x150.png" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" srcset="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/isa-1-150x150.png 150w, https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/isa-1-75x75.png 75w" sizes="(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-name">Garba Isa </div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-company">Student - North-East II, Bogoro, Incubatee</div><div class="clear"></div></div></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial testimonial t-slide post-4541"><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-inner testimonial-inner"><div data-infinite-loop="true"  class="wpmtst-testimonial-content  testimonial-content"><p>I want to gratefully appreciate the efforts of the Directorate for Entrepreneurship and General Studies especially on the rigorous training and encouragement received while undergoing the GST courses. These courses boosted my confidence and entrepreneurial skills and laid the foundation in me to become self-sufficient after graduation as well as enable me create sustainable jobs for others. I remain grateful to NOUN for this and many more achievements.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-image testimonial-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/timoty-1-150x150.png" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" srcset="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/timoty-1-150x150.png 150w, https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/timoty-1-75x75.png 75w" sizes="(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-name">Timothy Manasseh Garkuwa</div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-company">Student - North-East II, Bogoro, Incubatee</div><div class="clear"></div></div></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial testimonial t-slide post-9501"><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-inner testimonial-inner"><div data-infinite-loop="true"  class="wpmtst-testimonial-content  testimonial-content"><p>There is a proverb that says, “it takes a village to raise a child”. Tongues and Theatre Enterprise (TATE) is my child and I am grateful that the National Open University of Nigeria ( NOUN) is that village committed to its growth. I am grateful for members of that village- the Vice Chancellor: Prof. Olufemi Peters, the Director: Prof. Juliet Inegbedion, the Coordinator of the North Central Incubation Centre: Dr. Basil Ibebunjo and everyone on their teams. May this child grow and make its parents and the village proud. Amen</p></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-image testimonial-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095018-150x150.png" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" srcset="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095018-150x150.png 150w, https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095018-75x75.png 75w" sizes="(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-name">Priscilla Ajibola</div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-company">Student - North-Central, Abuja, Incubatee</div><div class="clear"></div></div></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial testimonial t-slide post-9503"><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-inner testimonial-inner"><div data-infinite-loop="true"  class="wpmtst-testimonial-content  testimonial-content"><p>I would like to express my profound gratitude and appreciation to the National Open University of Nigeria for the opportunity given me to showcase my business. It is a privilege to be among the top 3 and this is an experience I will cherish for a very long time. NOUN is a great institution, especially for given young enterprenuers the platform to grow.</p></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-image testimonial-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095356-150x150.png" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" srcset="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095356-150x150.png 150w, https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095356-75x75.png 75w, https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095356.png 296w" sizes="(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-name">Solomon Esther Tam Inioribi</div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-company">Student - South-West, Lagos, Incubatee</div><div class="clear"></div></div></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial testimonial t-slide post-9505"><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-inner testimonial-inner"><div data-infinite-loop="true"  class="wpmtst-testimonial-content  testimonial-content"><p>NOUN academic programme is very fantastic; NOUN has put smiles on my face as the institution has enabled me to realize my dream’. Otogor, a 400-level Accounting student, stated this on Monday, January 16, 2023, while receiving her award of one million naira (N1,000,000.00) for her creative product-based project at the Vice-Chancellor&#8217;s office, NOUN headquarters, Jabi Abuja. Otogor who designed the NOUN-customized laboratory coat said she was motivated by her passion for fashion design also to become an employer of labor after graduation</p></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-image testimonial-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095030-150x150.png" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" srcset="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095030-150x150.png 150w, https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095030-75x75.png 75w, https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095030.png 297w" sizes="(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-name">Mary Onyinye Otogor</div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-company">Student - North - Central Incubation Centre , Abuja Incubatee</div><div class="clear"></div></div></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial testimonial t-slide post-9507"><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-inner testimonial-inner"><div data-infinite-loop="true"  class="wpmtst-testimonial-content  testimonial-content"><p>My course on Entrepreneurship Education taught me how to write business plan and helped awaken my creativity and I was able to develop one of my ideas which is knitting. Through the mentorship of the Directorate, I won a 1 million Naira grant from the Tony Elumelu Foundation’s Entrepreneurship programme which I used to establish my business.</p></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-image testimonial-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095039-150x150.png" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" srcset="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095039-150x150.png 150w, https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095039-75x75.png 75w" sizes="(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-name">Bosede Alabi</div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-company">Student - North-Central, Abuja, Incubatee</div><div class="clear"></div></div></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial testimonial t-slide post-9509"><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-inner testimonial-inner"><div data-infinite-loop="true"  class="wpmtst-testimonial-content  testimonial-content"><p>I was encouraged to showcase my passion in Digital entertainment after undergoing training from DE&amp; GS, NOUN. I want to thank the management of NOUN for sponsoring my trip to Abuja to participate at the Nile University Entrepreneurship Trade Fair where I received an award from the Director of Abuja Enterprise Agency, as the winner of ‘Digital Media &amp; Entertainment’ of the fair.</p></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-image testimonial-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="150" height="150" src="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095055-150x150.png" class="attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" srcset="https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095055-150x150.png 150w, https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095055-75x75.png 75w, https://nou.edu.ng/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Screenshot-2024-04-04-095055.png 296w" sizes="(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px" /></div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-name">Obinna F. Nwanuo (2019) South-West, Lagos, Incubatee</div><div class="wpmtst-testimonial-field testimonial-field testimonial-company">Student - South-West, Lagos, Incubatee</div><div class="clear"></div></div></div></div></div></div>
			</div>
